# ==============================================================================
# Captain Cronos Shell Toolkit Prompt Template
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Template    : workflow
# Title       : Workflow
# Description : Render an operational workflow prompt.
# Order       : 40
# Version     : 1.0.0-alpha1
# Category    : Prompt
# Author      : Captain Cronos Project
# Tags        : workflow, operations, process
# Validation  : question-rules
# Default     : question defaults
# Examples    : workflow_name, trigger, safety_rules
# Output      : markdown
# Clipboard   : planned
# Repository  : CaptainCronos-01-ShellToolkit
# Purpose     : Render an operational workflow prompt.
# ==============================================================================

[questions]
workflow_name|text|yes|Workflow name||Short workflow name.||Prompt template release
trigger|textarea|yes|Trigger||When and why the workflow runs.||Before cutting a toolkit release.
steps|textarea|yes|Steps||Expected sequence of actions.||Run validation, review docs, commit changes.
safety_rules|textarea|yes|Safety rules||Dry-run, confirmation, rollback, or mutation constraints.||Do not merge to main before review.
validation|textarea|yes|Validation||Commands or checks that must pass.||cc install --dry-run

[template]
# Workflow Prompt

Workflow:
{{workflow_name}}

Trigger:
{{trigger}}

Steps:
{{steps}}

Safety rules:
{{safety_rules}}

Implementation guidance:
- Keep destructive or remote-mutating behavior guarded by explicit apply flags.
- Use existing shared logging, status, context, and dependency helpers.
- Preserve rollback paths when user files or operational state can change.
- Make dry-run behavior clear and verifiable.

Validation:
{{validation}}
